  "ordination": {
    "article_body_child_index": 55,
    "article_paragraph": "Three ordinations of the published Pf8 genotype-distance submatrix for the 1,900 isolates were compared (Fig. 2). UMAP achieved a trustworthiness of 0.486 and a Spearman correlation of 0.029 between embedded and original distances (McInnes et al. 2018); t-SNE reached 0.507 and 0.115; PCoA reached 0.495 and 0.322. PCoA preserves global distance structure best, while all three embeddings discard most of it. Silhouette coefficients computed by zone are negative in every case: -0.0156 on the original distances, -0.306 for UMAP, -0.057 for t-SNE and -0.112 for PCoA. Isolates are on average closer to members of other zones than to members of their own, in the original distance space as well as in each embedding. Zone-coloured isolates overlap extensively in Fig. 2, and no method recovers zone as a cluster boundary.",
